# Copy to .env and fill in. No real secrets in git (ADR-0025).
# Dedicated least-privilege role + database (not the postgres superuser).
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://fsm:<password>@localhost:5432/fsm?schema=public"
# Required. Boot aborts (#98) if unset, left as the old "dev-access-secret-change-me" default, or
# shorter than 32 chars. Generate one with: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('base64url'))"
JWT_ACCESS_SECRET="change-me-to-a-random-32+char-secret"

# ── Test database (isolated) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The vitest e2e suite runs against a SIBLING database, never DATABASE_URL directly: once a real
# AutoPlant sync has loaded the production org graph (~17.9k devices) into your dev DB, full-fleet
# operations (DeviceStateService.recompute, fleet-uptime aggregation) iterate every row and exceed
# the per-test timeout. By default the suite derives the test URL from DATABASE_URL by suffixing the
# db name with `_test` (…/fsm → …/fsm_test); set TEST_DATABASE_URL to override. test/global-setup.ts
# migrates + seeds it automatically before the run — but the database itself is a ONE-TIME superuser
# bootstrap (it needs the PostGIS extension, which the app role cannot create). As a Postgres
# superuser, once per machine:
#   CREATE DATABASE fsm_test OWNER fsm;
#   \c fsm_test
#   CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS postgis;
#   GRANT ALL ON SCHEMA public TO fsm;
# TEST_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://fsm:<password>@localhost:5432/fsm_test?schema=public"
#
# Every vitest run truncates + reseeds this database automatically (test/global-setup.ts, #180 R2) so
# no orphaned row from a crashed prior run survives into the next one. To reset it by hand (e.g. to
# inspect a clean baseline, or after a manual `psql` edit) without running the suite, build once, then:
#   pnpm build && pnpm test:reset

# ── AutoPlant upstream — read-only MySQL Snapshot source (Issue 04), reachable over VPN ──────────
# Least-privilege READ-ONLY account. Leave UNSET in dev / test / CI: the app boots without it and the
# SnapshotIngestionWorker keeps using its in-memory reader until the real SourceReader is wired.
# Set these in your local .env (never commit real secrets — ADR-0025) and connect to the VPN, then
# verify with: npm run build && npm run autoplant:ping
# The production source spans TWO databases on one host: ap_widgets (live telemetry — tb_vehiclemaster)
# and ap_masters (mst_* masters). BOTH must be set or the app stays on the in-memory reader.
# AUTOPLANT_MYSQL_HOST="10.0.0.25"         # private host — only resolvable/reachable on the VPN
# AUTOPLANT_MYSQL_PORT="3306"
# AUTOPLANT_MYSQL_USER="fsm_readonly"
# AUTOPLANT_MYSQL_PASSWORD="<password>"
# AUTOPLANT_MYSQL_DB_WIDGETS="ap_widgets"  # live telemetry schema (connection default)
# AUTOPLANT_MYSQL_DB_MASTERS="ap_masters"  # master-data schema (queried schema-qualified)
# AUTOPLANT_MYSQL_SSL="false"              # "true" if the server requires TLS
# (legacy AUTOPLANT_MYSQL_DATABASE still works as a fallback for AUTOPLANT_MYSQL_DB_WIDGETS)

# ── Ingestion scheduler (Issue 97 Slice 7) — in-process @nestjs/schedule cron ────────────────────
# OFF by default; enabling is a deliberate ops step AFTER zones are ratified (review B8). Dormant
# whenever AutoPlant is unconfigured (above), so dev/test/CI never need the VPN. Overlapping ticks
# degrade to a logged RUN_IN_PROGRESS skip — the in-flight guards stay the serialization mechanism.
# INGESTION_SCHEDULER_ENABLED="true"       # anything but the literal "true" stays OFF
# INGESTION_MASTERS_CRON="0 2 * * *"       # org-graph refresh — daily, off-hours
# INGESTION_TELEMETRY_CRON="*/30 * * * *"  # snapshot ingest + device-state recompute
# INGESTION_STALE_RUN_MIN="30"             # reap RUNNING runs older than this (Slice 2, review A2)
# INGESTION_RECON_MAX_DRIFT="0"            # rows of source-vs-FSM drift tolerated in /health (Slice 5)
# INGESTION_LIFECYCLE_QUIET_RUNS="3"       # consecutive syncs moving no device before /health warns (#218a).
#                                          # Patience, NOT tolerance: lifecycle `drift` has no acceptable
#                                          # non-zero value, so there is deliberately no knob for it.

# ── Business-sweep scheduler (Issue 108) / partition maintenance — the other two master switches ──
# BUSINESS_SWEEPS_ENABLED gates the periodic verification/intraday/cross-zone/report-cube sweeps
# (BusinessSweepSchedulerService); PARTITION_MAINTENANCE_ENABLED gates daily raw_device_snapshots
# partition creation. Both OFF by default, same "anything but the literal 'true' stays OFF" rule.
# BUSINESS_SWEEPS_ENABLED="true"
# PARTITION_MAINTENANCE_ENABLED="true"
#
# #182 — the e2e suite NEVER reads these (or any AUTOPLANT_MYSQL_*/INGESTION_*/PARTITION_*/
# BUSINESS_SWEEP* var) from this file. `test/setup-env.ts` is an ALLOWLIST: it deletes every var in
# the application's own namespace and re-sets a fixed test value for the handful the suite needs — so
# a NEW switch added here is neutralised automatically, by default, with no test-harness edit
# required. A spec that genuinely needs one ON passes it through the service's own config-override
# constructor param, never the environment (see #182 R5).

# ── Operations Data Explorer (#217) — read-only investigation surface ────────────────────────────
# OH-only, and additionally gated by OPS_EXPLORER_ENABLED. OFF by default in EVERY environment: this
# is a diagnostic instrument, not a product feature, so it is opted into per deployment. When off,
# every /api/ops-explorer/* route returns 404 (not 403 — a disabled feature should not confirm its
# own existence) and the admin nav entry does not render.
# OPS_EXPLORER_ENABLED="true"
#
# The lineage/diagnostics layer on top: source columns, the SQL that ran, bound parameters, query
# timings, raw responses. Defaults ON outside production and OFF when NODE_ENV=production; set it
# explicitly to override in either direction. It is stripped SERVER-SIDE — with it off the deep
# fields are absent from the JSON, so the browser never receives them. Implies OPS_EXPLORER_ENABLED:
# developer mode can never be on while the feature itself is off.
# OPS_EXPLORER_DEVELOPER_MODE="true"
